    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265-a3">

                <pb facs="0473" n="1433" sameAs="frus:frus1888p2/pg1433"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3 in No.
                    262.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Receipt of the collector of customs.</hi></head>
                <p rendition="#flush">Don José Ruiz Gaitero, 5th administrative officer, collector
                    of customs at this port, acting collector.</p>
                <p>I certify that Don Alejo Girond, consignee of the American schooner <hi
                        rendition="#italic">J. W. Parker</hi>, J. W. Kane, captain, has paid at this
                    subaltern office the sum of $361.14, for amount of tonnage dues of said vessel,
                    at the rate of $1 per ton, according to regulation 6, for which payment the
                    corresponding receipt was given to him.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">And at the request of the interested party,
                        and for the ends that may ensue, I issue these presents at <placeName>Tunas
                            de Zaza</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-12-27">this
                            27th day of December, 1887</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">José Ruiz</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Acting Collector.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
